\f2\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Analysis:
\f1\b0  The text lists physical body configurations banned from receiving monastic ordination: individuals with goiters (
\f3\i galaga\uc0\u7751 \u7693 a
\f1\i0 ), the mute, the deaf, and crucially, the 
\f4\b\fs28 p\uc0\u299 \u7789 hasarp\u299 
\f1\b0\fs32  (literally "one who crawls or slides on a platform/low stool" \'97 a contortionist or paraplegic street performer). It then issues a strict caste restriction: do not ordain chariot makers, 
\f4\b\fs28 ca\uc0\u7751 \u7693 \u257 las
\f1\b0\fs32 , or 
\f4\b\fs28 pukkasas
\f1\b0\fs32  (another heavily low-caste itinerant group).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Argument:
\f1\b0  This is direct evidence of institutional exclusion based on somatic and social attributes. Monastic institutions (both Buddhist and Brahmanical) were intensely anxious about the infiltration of unrefined, highly physical, street-performing bodies into their ranks. They explicitly paired outcaste designations (
\f3\i ca\uc0\u7751 \u7693 \u257 la
\f1\i0 , 
\f3\i pukkasa
\f1\i0 ) with physical contortion categories (
\f3\i p\uc0\u299 \u7789 hasarp\u299 
\f1\i0 ) to bar them from entering monastic spaces.\
